/* zh-SG translation source for "lessons" (generated by tools/i18n-pack.js; keys are the English source). */
Object.assign(window.I18N['zh-SG'].text, {
  "Notice the small things": "留意小事",
  "Sincere care often looks ordinary — a lunchbox, a remembered detail, someone waiting at your door. A specific \"thank you\" tells the other person their effort was seen, and that is how trust grows.": "真诚的关心往往看起来很平凡：一个便当、一个被记住的细节、有人在门口等你。一句具体的“谢谢”，会让对方知道他们的心意被看见了，信任就是这样建立起来的。",
  "Be where you are": "人在哪里，心就在哪里",
  "Scrolling while someone talks to you says \"you are less interesting than my screen\". Attention is the cheapest gift you can give, and the easiest one to forget.": "别人跟你说话时你在滑手机，等于在说“你没有我的屏幕有趣”。专注是你能给出最便宜的礼物，也是最容易被遗忘的礼物。",
  "Teasing runs on trust": "开玩笑需要信任",
  "Light teasing can be affectionate between people who already trust each other. Watch their reaction: if they stop smiling, the joke is over.": "在已经互相信任的人之间，轻松的玩笑可以是一种亲昵。留意对方的反应：如果他们不笑了，这个玩笑就该结束了。",
  "Love bombing": "爱情轰炸",
  "\"Soulmate\", \"destiny\", \"I have never felt this way\" — within minutes of meeting? Overwhelming flattery and rushing is a technique to lower your guard, not proof of love. Real interest survives a slower pace.": "才认识几分钟，就说“灵魂伴侣”、“命中注定”、“我从来没有过这种感觉”？铺天盖地的奉承和急于推进，是一种让你放下戒心的手段，不是爱的证明。真正的好感，经得起慢一点的节奏。",
  "Romance + money = alarm": "爱情 + 钱 = 警报",
  "\"Pig-butchering\" scams start with charm, then introduce an investment app, a crypto tip or an emergency. Never send money or \"invest\" because of someone you just met — online or in person.": "“杀猪盘”骗局从魅力开始，然后介绍一个投资应用、一条加密货币内幕或者一场紧急状况。永远不要因为一个刚认识的人而转钱或“投资”，不管是网上认识还是当面认识的。",
  "Let it grow at its own pace": "让它按自己的节奏成长",
  "Getting to know someone takes time and many small conversations. It is fine — attractive, even — to say \"let's get to know each other first.\"": "认识一个人需要时间，需要很多次小小的对话。说一句“我们先互相认识吧”完全没问题，甚至很有魅力。",
  "Read the signals": "读懂信号",
  "Short answers, eyes on the book, turning away: these mean \"not right now\". Interest looks like questions back and open body language. Giving space is not losing — it is respect.": "简短的回答、眼睛盯着书、转过身去：这些意思是“现在不要”。有兴趣的样子是会反问你问题、身体语言是开放的。给对方空间不是输了，是尊重。",
  "Touch needs a yes": "触碰需要“愿意”",
  "Grabbing someone's hand to \"help them stop being shy\" is not romantic; it ignores their choice. Touch, closeness and intimacy always need a clear, freely given yes — and \"no\" or silence is never a yes.": "抓住别人的手来“帮他们不再害羞”并不浪漫；那是无视了对方的选择。触碰、亲近和亲密，永远都需要一个清楚、自愿的“愿意”，而“不”或沉默永远都不是“愿意”。",
  "Don't mock what they love": "别嘲笑对方热爱的东西",
  "Laughing at someone's hobby is a quick way to make them close up. Curiosity (\"what do you like about it?\") opens people up.": "嘲笑别人的爱好，是让对方迅速封闭自己的方法。好奇心（“你喜欢它哪一点？”）才能让人敞开心扉。",
  "Hot & cold is a hook": "忽冷忽热是一个鱼钩",
  "Warm one day, cold the next, then a little reward — this \"intermittent reinforcement\" keeps you chasing. The rush you feel is anxiety, not chemistry. Consistency is what love actually looks like.": "今天热情，明天冷淡，然后给一点小甜头：这种“间歇性强化”会让你一直追下去。你感到的那股冲动是焦虑，不是化学反应。稳定，才是爱真正的样子。",
  "Calm and clear beats clever": "冷静清楚，胜过耍小聪明",
  "Say what happened and what you need, without insults: \"I waited 30 minutes. I like spending time with you, but I need plans to be real.\" Clear words earn respect; silent resentment doesn't.": "说出发生了什么、你需要什么，不带侮辱：“我等了30分钟。我喜欢跟你在一起，但我需要约好的计划是真的。”清楚的话能赢得尊重；默默的怨恨不能。",
  "Mind games breed mind games": "心理游戏只会招来心理游戏",
  "Making someone jealous or \"punishing\" them with silence might feel like winning, but it builds a relationship on tactics. You get back exactly what you play.": "让别人吃醋，或者用冷战来“惩罚”对方，也许感觉像是赢了，但这是在用手段建立一段关系。你玩什么，就会得到什么。",
  "Are you a backup?": "你是备胎吗？",
  "Someone who only messages when they need a favour, calls you \"the only one who gets me\", and keeps several \"besties\" on standby may be keeping a fish pond. Kindness is good; being a free service is not.": "一个只在需要帮忙时才找你、说你是“唯一懂我的人”、同时又养着好几个“闺蜜”备用的人，可能是在养鱼塘。善良是好事；但当一个免费服务就不是了。",
  "You may ask where you stand": "你可以问清楚自己的位置",
  "Helping is fine. Being used is not. You can offer what you are comfortable with, decline the rest, and simply ask: \"What are we?\" A good partner can handle that question.": "帮忙没关系。被利用就不行了。你可以提供你愿意给的，拒绝其他的，然后简单地问一句：“我们算什么？”一个好的对象，接得住这个问题。",
  "Flooding isn't love": "信息轰炸不是爱",
  "Fourteen messages in ten minutes does not show devotion — it shows panic, and it pushes people away. Feel the jealousy, then breathe, then talk once, calmly.": "十分钟发十四条信息，并不代表深情，只代表恐慌，而且会把人推开。感受那份嫉妒，然后深呼吸，然后冷静地谈一次。",
  "Self-respect is attractive": "自尊是有魅力的",
  "People treat you the way you allow. Having your own time, plans and limits is not \"playing hard to get\" — it is being a whole person someone can actually love.": "你允许别人怎么对待你，别人就会怎么对待你。有自己的时间、计划和界线，不是“欲擒故纵”，而是做一个完整的、别人能真正去爱的人。",
  "Curiosity beats a monologue": "好奇胜过独白",
  "People feel liked when you are interested in them, not when you are interesting at them. Ask, listen, then ask a follow-up about what they just said.": "当你对别人感兴趣时，对方会觉得被喜欢；而不是当你对着别人表现自己有多有趣时。提问，倾听，然后就对方刚说的话再追问一句。",
  "Negging is manipulation": "打压式搭讪是操控",
  "\"Backhanded\" compliments meant to lower someone's confidence are a pick-up-artist trick. It might get a reaction, but it builds nothing except distrust. Compliment what someone does or chooses, sincerely.": "故意贬低对方自信的“明褒暗贬”，是搭讪艺术家（PUA）的伎俩。它也许能引起反应，但除了不信任之外什么都建立不了。真诚地称赞一个人做了什么、选择了什么。",
  "You can't buy a connection": "感情买不来",
  "Spending big to impress makes people feel obliged, not close, and it trains you to believe you have to pay to be liked. Thoughtful beats expensive, every time.": "为了让人印象深刻而大手笔花钱，会让人觉得有负担，而不是亲近；也会让你习惯相信，必须付钱才能被喜欢。用心永远胜过昂贵。",
  "Don't use people to make others jealous": "别利用别人来让人吃醋",
  "Flirting with one person to get a reaction from another hurts both of them. If you like someone, show it to them directly.": "跟一个人调情，好让另一个人有反应，会同时伤害他们两个。如果你喜欢某个人，就直接让对方知道。",
  "Mocking friends isn't cool": "嘲笑朋友一点都不酷",
  "Putting a friend down to look good in front of others shows everyone how you'll treat them too. Laugh with people, not at them.": "为了在别人面前显得厉害而贬低朋友，等于让所有人都看到你以后会怎么对待他们。跟人一起笑，而不是笑人。",
  "\"Only I understand you\"": "“只有我懂你”",
  "Someone who tells you your friends and family are against you, and wants you all to themselves, is isolating you. Healthy partners want you to have a life full of people.": "一个告诉你你的朋友和家人都在跟你作对、想要独占你的人，是在孤立你。健康的伴侣会希望你的生活里有很多人。",
  "Don't compare": "别拿来比较",
  "Talking about how attractive other people are, or comparing someone to an ex, makes them feel like an option, not a choice.": "谈论别人有多好看，或者拿对方跟前任比较，会让对方觉得自己只是一个选项，而不是你的选择。",
  "One message is enough": "一条信息就够了",
  "\"Seen\" is not a verdict. People sleep, study, and have lives. Send one message, then put the phone down. Your calm is attractive; your flood is not.": "“已读”不是判决。人会睡觉、读书，也有自己的生活。发一条信息，然后放下手机。你的冷静有魅力；你的信息轰炸没有。",
  "Private chats stay private": "私聊就留在私聊里",
  "Screenshotting someone's messages for your friends breaks trust, and screenshots always travel further than you think.": "把别人的信息截图给朋友看会破坏信任，而且截图永远传得比你想象的更远。",
  "Sextortion: stop, don't pay, tell someone": "性勒索：停下来，不付钱，告诉别人",
  "Fake profiles flirt fast, ask for a private photo, then threaten to share it unless you pay. Never send. If it already happened: don't pay, keep the evidence, block, report, and tell a trusted adult. It is not your fault, and you are not alone.": "假账号会很快开始调情，要一张私密照片，然后威胁说除非你付钱，否则就公开。永远不要发。如果已经发生了：不要付钱，保留证据，封锁，举报，然后告诉一个信得过的大人。这不是你的错，你并不孤单。",
  "Urgent + money + secret = scam": "紧急 + 钱 + 秘密 = 骗局",
  "A sudden emergency, a tight deadline, and \"you're the only one I can trust\" is the classic shape of a money scam. Real emergencies have real families, hospitals and social workers.": "突如其来的紧急状况、很紧的期限，加上“你是我唯一能信任的人”，就是金钱骗局的经典模样。真正的紧急状况，会有真正的家人、医院和社工。",
  "Remembering is love": "记得，就是爱",
  "Birthdays, a favourite snack, the name of their book series — remembering small details shows someone they live in your mind, not just your calendar.": "生日、最喜欢的零食、他们在看的系列小说的名字：记得这些小细节，会让对方知道他们住在你心里，而不只是在你的日历上。",
  "Support, don't take over": "支持，而不是接管",
  "When someone is scared, standing beside them helps more than doing it for them. Let them be the hero of their own moment.": "当一个人害怕的时候，站在他身边，比替他做更有帮助。让他们成为自己那一刻的英雄。",
  "The rescuer trap": "拯救者陷阱",
  "Wanting to save someone with money or by fighting their battles alone feels heroic, but it often feeds the trap they're in. Real help means boundaries and connecting them to people who can actually help.": "想用钱去拯救一个人，或者独自替他打所有的仗，感觉很英勇，但往往只会让他困得更深。真正的帮助，是保持界线，并把他们和真正能帮上忙的人联系起来。",
  "Be honest about where you're at": "诚实说出你现在的状态",
  "It's normal to get to know several people at the start. It's not okay to tell each of them they're the only one. Honesty early saves everyone pain later.": "刚开始的时候同时认识几个人是正常的。但跟每个人都说“你是唯一”就不行了。早点诚实，就能省去所有人以后的痛苦。",
  "Don't corner someone in public": "别在公开场合逼人表态",
  "A big public confession puts the other person under pressure to say yes. Confess privately, simply, and make it easy for them to answer honestly.": "一场盛大的公开告白，会让对方承受说“好”的压力。私下、简单地告白，让对方容易诚实地回答。",
  "Take \"no\" with grace": "优雅地接受“不”",
  "\"No\" is an answer, not an opening offer. Being kind about rejection — no guilt-trips, no \"after all I did for you\" — is the clearest proof that you were a good person to like.": "“不”是一个答案，不是讨价还价的开价。被拒绝时保持善意：不让对方内疚，不说“我为你做了那么多”，这就是最清楚的证明，证明你是一个值得被喜欢的人。",
  "Don't stop trying after \"yes\"": "说了“好”之后也别停止努力",
  "The effort you put in to get together is the effort that keeps you together. A relationship is not a finish line.": "你为了在一起所付出的努力，正是让你们继续在一起的努力。一段关系不是终点线。",
  "Slow down": "慢下来",
  "\"I love you\" in week one, future kids' names, demands to go public — rushing puts pressure on something that needs time to grow roots.": "第一个星期就说“我爱你”、给未来的孩子取名、要求公开关系：急于推进，会给一个需要时间扎根的东西施加压力。",
  "What happens between you stays between you": "你们之间的事，就留在你们之间",
  "Bragging (or lying) to friends about your partner turns them into a story for your status. Privacy is a form of respect.": "向朋友炫耀（或吹嘘）你的另一半，会把对方变成你用来抬高身份的故事。隐私是一种尊重。",
  "Keep your own life": "保持你自己的生活",
  "Your friends, hobbies and goals don't disappear when you fall in love. Two whole people make a stronger couple than two halves.": "你的朋友、爱好和目标，不会因为你谈恋爱就消失。两个完整的人，比两个“半个人”组成的情侣更坚固。",
  "Feel jealousy, don't act it out": "感受嫉妒，但别把它演出来",
  "Jealousy is a normal feeling, not a fact. Notice it, calm down, then talk about it honestly instead of sulking, accusing or confronting.": "嫉妒是一种正常的感受，而不是事实。察觉它，冷静下来，然后诚实地谈一谈，而不是闹脾气、指责或者对质。",
  "Don't go through their phone": "别翻对方的手机",
  "Reading someone's messages or tracking them destroys trust faster than anything you could find. If you can't trust them, talk — or leave.": "偷看别人的信息或追踪对方的位置，摧毁信任的速度比你能找到的任何东西都快。如果你没办法信任对方，就谈一谈，或者离开。",
  "Control isn't care": "控制不是关心",
  "Demanding passwords, constant location sharing, or telling someone who they can see are controlling behaviours, whatever \"alpha\" videos say.": "要求对方交出密码、一直共享位置，或者规定对方可以见谁，这些都是控制行为，不管那些“阿尔法男”视频怎么说。",
  "No double standards": "不要双重标准",
  "If you expect openness from your partner, offer it first. Rules that only apply to them aren't rules; they're control.": "如果你希望另一半对你坦白，就先对他坦白。只对对方适用的规则不是规则，是控制。",
  "Celebrate their wins": "为对方的成就喝彩",
  "A good partner is happy when you shine. If their success makes you feel small, that's your feeling to work on — not their light to dim.": "一个好的伴侣，会在你发光时感到高兴。如果对方的成功让你觉得自己很渺小，那是你需要处理的感受，而不是要对方把光调暗。",
  "Listen before you fix": "先听，再想办法",
  "When someone vents, they often need to be heard before they need solutions. Ask: \"Do you want advice, or do you want me to just listen?\"": "当一个人在倾诉时，他们往往需要先被听见，然后才需要解决办法。问一问：“你想要建议，还是只想要我听你说？”",
  "A real apology": "一个真正的道歉",
  "Name what you did, own it without \"but\", say how it affected them, and ask how to make it right. \"Sorry you feel that way\" is not an apology.": "说出你做了什么，不加“但是”地承认，说出这对对方造成了什么影响，然后问要怎么弥补。“很抱歉你这样觉得”不是道歉。",
  "Don't dismiss feelings": "别否定对方的感受",
  "\"You're overreacting\" and \"you're crazy\" end the conversation and start the resentment. You don't have to agree to say \"I can see this hurt you.\"": "“你反应过度了”和“你疯了”会结束对话，开始怨恨。你不需要同意，也可以说“我看得出这让你受伤了”。",
  "Pause, don't punish": "暂停，而不是惩罚",
  "Taking a break to cool down is healthy if you say when you'll come back. Days of silence as punishment is stonewalling.": "如果你说清楚什么时候回来，暂时离开冷静一下是健康的。用好几天的沉默来惩罚对方，就是冷暴力。",
  "Never threaten to leave to win a fight": "永远别用分手来赢得争吵",
  "\"Maybe we should just break up\" used as a weapon makes the relationship feel unsafe. Only say it if you mean it.": "把“也许我们干脆分手吧”当武器，会让这段关系变得不安全。只有在你是认真的时候才说。",
  "Say what you need": "说出你需要什么",
  "Nobody can read your mind. Expecting a partner to \"just know\" sets them up to fail. Ask for what you need clearly and kindly.": "没有人会读心术。期望另一半“自然就会懂”，就是在让对方注定失败。清楚而温和地说出你需要什么。",
  "Couples who last are couples who repair": "能走下去的情侣，是懂得修复的情侣",
  "Every couple fights. What matters is coming back afterwards, talking about what happened, and both changing a little.": "每一对情侣都会吵架。重要的是事后回到彼此身边，谈谈发生了什么，然后两个人都改变一点点。",
  "\"If you loved me…\" is pressure": "“如果你爱我……”是施压",
  "Guilt is not consent. \"Not yet\" is a complete answer, and respecting it builds the trust that real closeness needs.": "内疚不是同意。“还没准备好”是一个完整的答案，尊重它，就能建立真正亲密所需要的信任。",
  "Never ask for or share intimate images": "永远不要索取或分享私密照片",
  "Asking a partner for private photos pressures them, and sharing anyone's intimate image without consent is abuse — and for minors, a serious crime. If you see it happening, report it.": "向另一半要私密照片是在施压，而未经同意分享任何人的私密照片都是虐待，涉及未成年人更是严重的罪行。如果你看到这种事发生，就去举报。",
  "Love them the way they like to be loved": "用对方喜欢的方式去爱",
  "A \"romantic\" gesture they told you they dislike is about you, not them. Listen to what they actually enjoy.": "一个对方明明说过不喜欢的“浪漫”举动，是关于你自己，而不是关于对方。听听对方真正喜欢的是什么。",
  "Respect their people": "尊重对方身边的人",
  "Being kind and curious with your partner's friends and family shows you take their whole life seriously.": "对另一半的朋友和家人友善、好奇，会让对方知道你认真对待他的整个人生。",
  "No body jokes": "不拿身体开玩笑",
  "Joking about anyone's body for laughs hurts, and staying silent when friends do it teaches them it's fine. \"Not cool, man\" is enough.": "为了搞笑而拿任何人的身体开玩笑都会伤人，而朋友这样做时你保持沉默，就是在告诉他们这没关系。一句“兄弟，这样不好笑”就够了。",
  "Distance needs a rhythm, not a leash": "远距离需要节奏，不是牵绳",
  "Agree on how you'll stay in touch instead of demanding instant replies. Trust is what fills the gaps between messages.": "约好你们要怎么保持联络，而不是要求对方秒回。信任，就是填满信息之间空白的东西。",
  "Don't abandon yourself": "别抛弃你自己",
  "Dropping your studies, club and friends to be \"always available\" doesn't make you a better partner — it makes you resentful.": "为了“随时在线”而放弃学业、社团和朋友，不会让你成为更好的伴侣，只会让你心生怨恨。",
  "Small lies, big cracks": "小谎言，大裂痕",
  "A little lie to avoid an awkward talk teaches your partner that your words can't be trusted. Come clean early; it only gets more expensive.": "为了避开一场尴尬的谈话而撒一个小谎，会让另一半知道你的话不可信。早点坦白；拖得越久代价越大。",
  "Talk about money openly": "坦白地谈钱",
  "Choose things you can both afford, share fairly, and never use money as a scoreboard or a leash.": "选择你们两个都负担得起的事，公平分担，永远不要把钱当成记分板或牵绳。",
  "Be there — you don't have to fix it": "陪在身边：你不需要解决问题",
  "When someone is struggling, listening and staying close matters more than solutions. Encourage them to talk to a counsellor or trusted adult; you are support, not their therapist.": "当一个人正在挣扎时，倾听和陪伴比解决办法更重要。鼓励他们去找辅导员或信得过的大人谈谈；你是支持，不是他们的心理治疗师。",
  "End with respect": "带着尊重结束",
  "If someone ends things, begging, stalking or revenge only prove they were right. Grieve, lean on friends, and wish them well. A kind ending is still a good story.": "如果对方要结束这段关系，哀求、跟踪或报复，只会证明他们是对的。好好难过，依靠朋友，然后祝福对方。一个温柔的结局，依然是一个好故事。",
  "Love doesn't cage": "爱不是牢笼",
  "\"If you loved me you'd stay\" is a guilt-trip. Loving someone means wanting their dreams to come true, and figuring out the rest together.": "“如果你爱我，你就会留下”是一种情感勒索。爱一个人，就是希望他的梦想成真，然后一起想办法解决其他的事。",
  "Guys can support guys": "男生也可以支持男生",
  "Everyone falls for something. Being the friend who says \"it's okay, let's fix it\" instead of mocking is what real friendship looks like.": "每个人都会上当。当那个说“没关系，我们一起解决”而不是嘲笑他的朋友，这就是真正友情的样子。",
  "Honest beats impressive": "诚实胜过体面",
  "\"I don't know — tell me?\" wins over a confident wrong guess or a smooth lie. Honesty is the foundation everything else stands on.": "“我不知道，你可以告诉我吗？”胜过一个自信但错误的猜测或一个圆滑的谎言。诚实是其他一切的地基。",
  "Something that's yours": "属于你自己的东西",
  "A hobby you love for its own sake makes you steadier, more interesting and harder to manipulate. People who have their own thing don't need someone else to be their whole world.": "一个你纯粹因为热爱而投入的爱好，会让你更稳定、更有趣，也更难被操控。有自己热爱之事的人，不需要别人成为他的全世界。",
  "Pay yourself first": "先付钱给自己",
  "When money comes in, put a fixed slice aside before you spend anything: savings first, then needs, then fun. A small buffer is what lets you say no to pressure later.": "有钱进来时，先把固定的一部分存起来，再花其他的：先储蓄，再付必需品，最后才是娱乐。一点小小的缓冲，就是让你以后能对压力说“不”的东西。",
  "Paid attention is a product": "付费换来的关注是一种商品",
  "A streamer saying your name after a gift is a service, designed to make you gift again. Enjoy the show if you like it, but a shout-out is not a relationship, and you cannot buy your way into one.": "主播在你送礼物后念出你的名字，是一种服务，目的是让你再送一次。喜欢就享受这场表演，但一次点名不是一段关系，你也不可能用钱买到一段关系。",
  "\"No\" is a complete budget": "“不”就是一份完整的预算",
  "\"I can't afford that\" and \"That's not in my budget\" are full sentences. Someone who cares about you will not need you to prove your love with money you don't have.": "“我负担不起”和“这不在我的预算里”都是完整的句子。真正在乎你的人，不会需要你用你没有的钱来证明你的爱。",
  "Look at the total, not the monthly": "看总价，不是看月供",
  "\"Only $83 a month!\" is $998. Instalments make big prices feel small. Before buying, multiply it out, and ask what else that money could have been.": "“每月只需$83！”其实就是$998。分期付款会让大价钱感觉很小。买之前先乘一乘，再想想这笔钱原本还可以用来做什么。",
  "Family money is a team topic": "家里的钱是团队话题",
  "Contributing at home, or being helped by family, is normal. Talk openly about it, set a sum you can keep, and don't let guilt or pride decide for you.": "帮补家用，或者接受家人的帮助，都是正常的。坦白地谈，定一个你能持续的数额，别让内疚或面子替你做决定。",
  "Nobody wakes up filtered": "没有人醒来就自带滤镜",
  "Online faces are edited, lit and chosen from fifty shots. Comparing a real person, or yourself, to a filter is comparing life to an advert.": "网上的脸都经过修图、打光，还是从五十张里挑出来的。拿一个真实的人，或者你自己，去跟滤镜比较，就是拿生活去跟广告比较。",
  "Split the work, don't serve": "分担工作，而不是献殷勤",
  "At camp or at home, \"helping\" is doing your share, not hovering to impress someone. Shared work, done without being asked, is quietly very attractive.": "在营里或在家里，“帮忙”是做好你的那一份，而不是为了讨好某个人在旁边转来转去。不用别人开口就主动分担工作，其实非常有魅力。",
  "\"No thanks\" — and stay with your people": "“不用了，谢谢”，然后继续跟你的朋友在一起",
  "You can decline a drink, a dare or a plan and stay in the group. A clear \"no thanks\" with no long excuse is enough. Good friends move on; pushy ones show you who they are.": "你可以拒绝一杯酒、一个挑战或一个计划，同时继续留在团体里。一句清楚的“不用了，谢谢”，不需要长篇大论的理由，就够了。好朋友会接受；硬要逼你的人，会让你看清他们是什么样的人。",
  "You fell for your own imagination": "你爱上的是你自己的想象",
  "When you fill in someone with your own fantasy, you are dating a story in your head. The real person will always \"disappoint\" the story. Ask, listen and let them be who they are.": "当你用自己的幻想去填补一个人，你就是在跟脑海里的一个故事谈恋爱。真实的那个人，永远都会让那个故事“失望”。去问，去听，让对方做他自己。",
  "Lost? Stay, call, share location": "迷路了？待在原地、打电话、分享位置",
  "If you get separated outdoors: stop, stay where you are, call or message, and share your live location. Wandering off to be a hero makes rescues harder.": "如果在户外走散了：停下来，待在原地，打电话或发信息，分享你的实时位置。为了当英雄而到处乱走，只会让救援更困难。",
  "Polish isn't character": "光鲜不等于品格",
  "Confidence, a nice car and smooth words say nothing about how someone keeps promises. Watch what they do when it costs them something.": "自信、一辆好车和花言巧语，完全说明不了一个人会不会守承诺。看看当守承诺要付出代价时，他会怎么做。",
  "Keep your own stage": "守住你自己的舞台",
  "Support your partner's big moment, and keep building yours. Two people with their own stages are a team; one spotlight and one audience is a lopsided show.": "支持另一半的重要时刻，同时继续经营你自己的。两个各有舞台的人是一个团队；一个聚光灯配一个观众，是一场失衡的表演。",
  "Know vs. assumed": "知道的 vs. 假设的",
  "Before you react, separate what you know (\"she didn't reply\") from what you assume (\"she's with someone else\"). Most heartbreak is written in the assumption column.": "在做出反应之前，先把你知道的（“她没回复”）和你假设的（“她跟别人在一起”）分开。大部分的心碎，都写在“假设”那一栏里。",
  "She's a person, not a poster": "她是一个人，不是一张海报",
  "Behind the stream, the idol photo or the profile picture is a tired human who eats, worries and has bad days. Treat her like one: with respect, not worship.": "在直播、偶像照片或头像的背后，是一个会累、会吃饭、会担心、也会有糟糕日子的人。把她当人看：给予尊重，而不是崇拜。",
  "The screen doesn't love you back": "屏幕不会回爱你",
  "Feeling close to someone you watch every night is normal; it's how screens are built. But it runs one way. Real relationships need two people who both know each other.": "对一个你每天晚上都在看的人感到亲近是正常的；屏幕本来就是这样设计的。但那是单向的。真正的关系，需要两个互相了解的人。",
  "Status is marketing": "身份地位是一种营销",
  "\"Lambo or loser\" is an advert. Brands and influencers sell the feeling that you are not enough yet. Enjoy nice things you can afford, but never let a price tag tell you your worth.": "“不开兰博基尼就是废物”是一则广告。品牌和网红在卖给你一种“你还不够好”的感觉。享受你负担得起的好东西，但永远别让价格标签告诉你你值多少。",
  "Your evenings are your life": "你的夜晚就是你的人生",
  "Endless scrolling and watching takes the hours that would have become your skills, friendships and sleep. Choose where your attention goes, or the app will choose for you.": "无止境地滑手机、看视频，会吃掉那些本来可以变成你的技能、友情和睡眠的时间。你要选择自己的注意力去哪里，否则应用程序会替你选择。",
  "Like who she is, not how she looks": "喜欢她是谁，而不是她长什么样",
  "Attraction is real and fine. But looks change and fade; how someone treats people, keeps promises and laughs at herself is what you will actually live with.": "吸引力是真实的，也没有问题。但外表会改变、会褪色；一个人怎么待人、怎么守承诺、怎么自嘲，才是你真正要一起生活的东西。",
  "Good dates are cheap": "好的约会很便宜",
  "A walk at the park connector, hawker food, a free museum day: the best dates are about attention, not spending. Take turns paying, or split. Nobody owes anybody.": "在公园连道散步、吃小贩中心、博物馆免费日：最好的约会关乎用心，而不是花钱。轮流付，或者平分。谁都不欠谁。",
  "Your \"not yet\" counts too": "你的“还没准备好”也算数",
  "Boys get pressured as well, by friends, by \"what everyone is doing\", even by partners. You never owe anyone a step you are not ready for.": "男生也会被施压，来自朋友、来自“大家都在做”，甚至来自另一半。你永远不欠任何人一个你还没准备好的步骤。",
  "Facts, not myths: condoms protect against pregnancy and STIs": "事实，不是谣言：安全套能防止怀孕和性病",
  "Used correctly every time, condoms are the only contraception that also lowers the risk of STIs. Other methods (like the pill) prevent pregnancy but not infections. \"Pulling out\" and \"first time is safe\" are myths.": "每次都正确使用的话，安全套是唯一一种同时能降低性病风险的避孕方法。其他方法（比如避孕药）能防止怀孕，但不能防止感染。“体外射精”和“第一次很安全”都是谣言。",
  "STIs are serious — and often silent": "性病很严重，而且常常没有症状",
  "Many sexually transmitted infections have no symptoms for a long time but can still cause harm and be passed on. Testing is confidential, quick and normal. Most are treatable when found early.": "很多性传播感染在很长一段时间里都没有症状，但仍然会造成伤害，也会传给别人。检测是保密的、快速的，也很平常。大部分及早发现都能治疗。",
  "Risk is about what people do, not who they love": "风险取决于人们做了什么，而不是他们爱谁",
  "STI risk comes from behaviours, such as sex without a condom, many partners or not testing, not from anyone's orientation. Blaming a group spreads stigma, and stigma stops people getting tested.": "性病风险来自行为，比如不戴安全套、有多个性伴侣或不做检测，而不是来自任何人的性取向。怪罪某一个群体只会散播污名，而污名会让人不敢去检测。",
  "Pressure, choking, filming, getting someone drunk: red flags": "施压、掐脖子、偷拍、把人灌醉：都是红旗",
  "Pushing past a no, anything copied from porn like choking, filming without clear consent, or getting someone drunk \"to relax them\" are not romance. They are danger signs, and some are crimes.": "对方说了不还继续施压、模仿色情片里的掐脖子等行为、没有明确同意就拍摄，或者把人灌醉“让她放松”，这些都不是浪漫。它们是危险信号，有些还是罪行。",
  "Secret + gifts + isolation + photos = grooming": "秘密 + 礼物 + 孤立 + 照片 = 诱骗",
  "An older person who gives gifts, asks you to keep secrets, cuts you off from friends and asks for photos is grooming, whatever they call it. It is never your fault. Tell a trusted adult.": "一个年纪比你大的人送你礼物、叫你保守秘密、让你疏远朋友、还向你要照片，这就是诱骗，不管他们怎么称呼它。这永远不是你的错。告诉一个信得过的大人。",
  "Waiting is normal; stopping is strength": "等待是正常的；停下来是一种力量",
  "Most teens are not having sex, whatever the group chat says. Waiting is normal. Stopping at any moment, for any reason, is allowed and respected.": "大部分青少年都没有发生性行为，不管群里怎么说。等待是正常的。任何时候、因为任何原因停下来，都是被允许、被尊重的。",
  "Available isn't the same as loving": "随时在线不等于爱",
  "Being on call 24/7 for a partner can feel like love, but it can eat your sleep, studies and friendships. Real support includes keeping your own life running.": "二十四小时随时待命，可能感觉像爱，但它会吃掉你的睡眠、学业和友情。真正的支持，也包括让你自己的生活继续运转。",
  "Sleep is part of the plan": "睡眠是计划的一部分",
  "Exam season, heartbreak, a big game: everything goes better on seven to nine hours of sleep. Staying up all night is not dedication; it's a tax on tomorrow.": "考试季、失恋、一场大比赛：睡足七到九个小时，一切都会更顺利。熬通宵不是投入；那是向明天征的税。",
  "Bring a plan, not a slammed door": "带着计划去谈，而不是甩门",
  "When you disagree with your parents about your future, bring facts, a backup plan and respect. \"Here's what I want and how I'll make it work\" lands better than a door.": "当你和父母对你的未来意见不合时，带上事实、备用计划和尊重。“这是我想要的，以及我会怎么做到”比甩门有用得多。",
  "Heal forward": "向前疗伤",
  "After a breakup or a failure: sleep, eat, move, talk to a friend, and do one small thing for your future each day. Feelings pass faster when your life keeps moving.": "分手或失败之后：睡觉、吃饭、运动、找朋友聊聊，每天为你的未来做一件小事。当你的生活继续前进，感受也会过去得更快。",
  "Don't shrink your future for anyone": "别为了任何人缩小你的未来",
  "Choosing a course, a job or a country only to stay near someone is a big bet on one person. Make plans together, but don't delete your own dream to fit theirs.": "只为了留在某个人身边而选择一个科系、一份工作或一个国家，是把一切押在一个人身上。一起做计划，但别为了配合对方的梦想而删掉你自己的。",
  "Feed yourself first": "先养活自己",
  "Budget for food, transport and bills before anything else. An adult who can cook three meals and pay their own phone bill is far more attractive than any gift.": "先把伙食、交通和账单列进预算，然后才是其他的。一个会煮三顿饭、能自己付电话费的大人，比任何礼物都有魅力得多。",
  "Minimum payment, maximum trap": "最低还款，最大陷阱",
  "Credit cards and \"buy now, pay later\" charge high interest. Paying only the minimum can take years and cost far more than the thing. Avoid borrowing for wants.": "信用卡和“先买后付”的利息都很高。只付最低还款可能要还好几年，最后花的钱远远超过那样东西本身。别为了“想要”的东西借钱。",
  "Lend only what you can lose": "只借你输得起的钱",
  "If you lend money to a friend, treat it as a gift you might not get back. If losing it would hurt you or the friendship, say no kindly and help in another way.": "如果你借钱给朋友，就把它当成一份可能拿不回来的礼物。如果拿不回来会伤到你或你们的友情，就温和地拒绝，用别的方式帮忙。",
  "Asking for help is strength": "寻求帮助是一种力量",
  "Money trouble, stress, a dark week: telling someone early, a friend, family or a helpline, stops small problems from growing. Nobody gets through adult life alone.": "钱的问题、压力、灰暗的一周：早点告诉别人，朋友、家人或者热线，就能阻止小问题变大。没有人能独自撑过成年生活。",
  "Say no to the room": "对一整屋子的人说不",
  "In Singapore you have to be 18 to buy or drink alcohol in public places, and not drinking never needs an explanation. \"I'm good, thanks\" works on any dare. The right friends shrug and move on.": "在新加坡，你必须年满18岁才能购买酒类或在公共场所喝酒，而不喝酒永远不需要解释。“我这样就好，谢谢”对付任何挑战都有效。对的朋友会耸耸肩，然后就过去了。",
  "Step in, stay with her": "上前介入，陪着她",
  "If someone is too drunk or being pressured, don't walk away. Get a friend, stay with them, get them water and a safe ride, and call for help if needed. Nobody \"deserves\" to be left alone.": "如果有人醉得太厉害或正在被施压，不要走开。叫上一个朋友，陪着他们，给他们水，安排安全的交通，需要时就求救。没有人“活该”被丢下。",
  "Left it? Leave it": "放着没看？那就别喝了",
  "If your drink was left alone or tastes strange, don't finish it. Watch your friends' drinks too, and leave together.": "如果你的饮料曾经无人看管或者味道奇怪，就别喝完。也帮朋友看好他们的饮料，然后一起离开。",
  "Impulse isn't a plan": "冲动不是计划",
  "Big decisions made in a rush, after a fight, a drink or a dare, are usually the ones you regret. Sleep on it. A good choice will still be good tomorrow.": "在匆忙之中、吵架之后、喝了酒或被人怂恿时做的重大决定，通常就是你会后悔的那些。睡一觉再说。好的选择，明天依然是好的。",
  "Talk before you touch": "触碰之前先沟通",
  "Before any step, talk: what you both want, what you don't, and what protection you would use. If you can't talk about it, you're not ready to do it.": "任何一步之前，先谈：你们两个想要什么、不想要什么、会用什么保护措施。如果你没办法谈这件事，你就还没准备好做这件事。",
  "Protection is both partners' job": "保护措施是两个人的事",
  "Contraception and STI protection are never \"her problem\" or \"his problem\". Both partners plan, pay and take responsibility.": "避孕和预防性病永远都不是“她的问题”或“他的问题”。两个人一起计划、一起付钱、一起负责。",
  "No symptoms ≠ no STI": "没有症状 ≠ 没有性病",
  "You can't see an STI. Regular, confidential testing is how responsible adults look after themselves and their partners.": "性病是看不出来的。定期、保密的检测，是负责任的成年人照顾自己和另一半的方式。",
  "Yes can change to no": "“愿意”可以变成“不”",
  "Consent is ongoing. Someone can say yes and then change their mind at any time, and that change is respected immediately, with no guilt trip.": "同意是持续的。一个人可以先说愿意，然后在任何时候改变主意，而这个改变要立刻被尊重，不能让对方内疚。",
  "Your timeline is yours": "你的时间表是你自己的",
  "There is no correct age for a first kiss, a first relationship or anything else. Comparing your timeline to the group chat is comparing to rumours.": "初吻、第一段恋爱或其他任何事，都没有所谓正确的年龄。拿你的时间表去跟群聊比较，就是在跟谣言比较。",
  "Scare? Act fast, together": "出了状况？一起迅速行动",
  "If protection fails, act quickly and calmly. Emergency contraception works best the sooner it is taken; in Singapore she sees a GP or polyclinic doctor for it, and you can go with her. Share the cost, plan an STI test, support her decisions. Blame helps nobody; a plan does.": "如果保护措施失败了，就冷静、迅速地行动。紧急避孕越早服用效果越好；在新加坡，她需要去看家庭医生或综合诊疗所的医生，你可以陪她去。一起分担费用，安排性病检测，支持她的决定。指责帮不了任何人；计划才能。",
  "Romance + investing = scam": "爱情 + 投资 = 骗局",
  "Someone you met online who is charming, never video-calls and starts talking about crypto or a trading app is following a script. Never invest because of a romance.": "一个在网上认识、很有魅力、从来不视频通话、又开始谈加密货币或交易应用的人，是在照着剧本走。永远不要因为一段感情而投资。",
  "You can't buy someone's affection": "你买不到别人的感情",
  "\"Pay a deposit to meet me\", \"buy coins to unlock her chat\": paying to talk to someone is a business, and often a scam. Real people don't charge for their time with you.": "“付订金就能见我”、“买金币解锁她的聊天”：花钱跟人聊天是一门生意，而且往往是骗局。真实的人不会为了陪你而收费。",
  "\"Your friends hold you back\" is a script": "“你的朋友在拖你后腿”是一个剧本",
  "Schemes that pay mainly for recruiting, use pressure and tell you to cut off doubters are textbook. If people who love you are worried, listen.": "主要靠拉人头赚钱、施加压力、叫你跟质疑的人断绝来往的计划，就是教科书式的骗局。如果爱你的人在担心，就听听他们的话。",
  "Scams target people, not \"idiots\"": "骗局针对的是人，不是“白痴”",
  "Scams are made by professionals to beat smart people when they are tired, lonely or hopeful. If it happens to you or a friend, report it fast (ScamShield 1799) and drop the shame.": "骗局是专业的人设计出来的，专门在聪明人疲惫、寂寞或怀抱希望的时候打败他们。如果它发生在你或朋友身上，就迅速举报（ScamShield 1799），并且放下羞耻感。",
  "Different values aren't wrong values": "不同的价值观不是错误的价值观",
  "Saving or spending, a big family or none, family close by or far: these are preferences, not morals. Say yours honestly and ask about theirs. Different isn't a loss.": "储蓄还是花钱、大家庭还是不要孩子、住在家人附近还是远一点：这些是偏好，不是道德问题。诚实地说出你的，也问问对方的。不一样不代表输了。",
  "Agreeing to everything isn't love": "什么都附和不是爱",
  "If you agree with everything to keep someone, she ends up dating nobody, and you resent it later. Your view, said kindly, is part of what she's choosing.": "如果你为了留住一个人而附和一切，到最后她等于在跟一个不存在的人谈恋爱，而你以后也会心生怨恨。你的看法，温和地说出来，正是她所选择的你的一部分。",
  "Disagree without sneering": "可以不同意，但别冷嘲热讽",
  "Eye-rolling, mocking and \"that's stupid\" are contempt, one of the strongest predictors that a relationship will end. Attack the idea if you must; respect the person.": "翻白眼、嘲笑和“那很蠢”都是轻蔑，而轻蔑是预测一段关系会结束的最强指标之一。如果一定要，就攻击那个想法；但要尊重那个人。",
  "A kind \"this doesn't fit\" is allowed": "温柔地说“我们不合适”是可以的",
  "Some differences are too big to compromise on, like wanting children or not. Saying it early and kindly isn't failure; it's respect for both your futures.": "有些差异大到无法妥协，比如想不想要孩子。早点、温柔地说出来不是失败；而是对你们两个人未来的尊重。",
  "Some things aren't a matter of taste": "有些事不是品味的问题",
  "Lying that hides harm, fraud and breaking promises in silence aren't \"different values\". Keep an integrity floor, and notice who else keeps one.": "用来掩盖伤害的谎言、诈骗、默默打破承诺，都不是“不同的价值观”。守住诚信的底线，也留意身边还有谁守着它。",
  "Us vs. the problem": "我们 vs. 问题",
  "Housing prices, career pressure, family expectations: many fights between couples are really outside pressures. Name the pressure together before blaming each other.": "房价、事业压力、家人的期望：很多情侣之间的争吵，其实是来自外界的压力。在互相指责之前，先一起说出那个压力是什么。"
});
